“Mo Money Mo Problems” was recorded by The Notorious B.I.G. for his second album, Life After Death, released in 1997. The track features Puff Daddy and Mase and is built around a sample of Diana Ross’s “I’m Coming Out.” This hip hop song reached No. 1 on the Billboard Hot 100, becoming the second posthumous No. 1 single for The Notorious B.I.G. 

Directed by: Hype Williams

